    "updated_at": "2025-07-17T00:10:09Z",
    "body": "Ughhhh, no, this still violates LL(1). I misread the restriction - it's not that an *entire* production can't be a prefix to another production, it's that *no* two productions in an alternative can share a prefix.\r\n\r\nGuess it'll have to be `async_sequence<>`, then. :(",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
